Subject: rug uses bl default in ggplot but not qplot
Message-ID: <whmd6wCrxTQ.pt0IUc_rFs0J@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/whmd6wCrxTQ/m/pt0IUc_rFs0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi All,

I did a histogram with a rug in ggplot, and it worked fine:

> mydata <- data.frame(x=rnorm(100))

> ggplot(mydata, aes(x)) +
+ geom_histogram() +
+ geom_rug()
stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use 'binwidth = x' to adjust this.

Then I did it using qplot and it said "sides" has no default value. The help file says it's "bl".

> qplot(mydata$x, geom = c("histogram", "rug") )
stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use 'binwidth = x' to adjust this.
Error: argument "sides" is missing, with no default

When I specify "bl" it works:

> qplot(mydata$x, geom = c("histogram", "rug"), sides = "bl" )
stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use 'binwidth = x' to adjust this.

Is this a bug, or am I misunderstanding the code differences between ggplot and qplot?

Thanks,
Bob

